# The seam fixtures are encoder output, compared byte-for-byte by
# `tests/test_seam_fixture.py` and parsed byte-for-byte by
# `web/tests/seam.test.ts`. This repo is developed on Windows with
# `core.autocrlf=true`, where git rewrites line endings in any file it
# *guesses* is text. Both blobs happen to carry a NUL byte early enough for
# that guess to come out right today, but that is a property of the data
# currently in them, not of the format: a regenerated fixture that happened to
# hold no NUL in its first 8000 bytes would be silently CRLF-mangled on
# checkout, and the byte-identity test would fail on a machine whose author
# changed nothing.
web/tests/fixtures/*.bin binary
